From a5454b95ba53b0ffa2edf9a9fdfb859277c89063 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 22:58:01 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 6/7] MT-FIX1 (web): review fixes -- jog stop can no longer
 overtake the jog, window heartbeat survives alarm dialogs, Motor Power
 carries its direction, formShow/formClose reconciled, MotorTest.ini write
 safer

From the adversarial review of 8336746 / ef20fb8 / b4c613e (20260925), web side:
- HIGH: ht9045_recipe_client.js motorAccess sent motor.access only after the control.acquire ack while motorStop went
  out at once, so a quick tap could put motor.stop on the wire BEFORE the jog (axis jogs, nothing stops it).
  acquire + motor.access now go back to back (wire order = call order); the caller still gets control-held.
  motor-access.js: a jog ack that arrives after the button was released sends one more stop (late-ack);
  release() stops the motor that was jogged, not the one selected at release; releaseHeld() for hidden frames.
- HIGH: HT9045Windows.put latched "unsupported" on ANY refusal, so the first heartbeat refused with modal-pending
  during an alarm dialog stopped the registry for good -> after 15 s C++ saw Motor Test/Teach as open (MainProc
  pause stuck). Only "unknown cmd" latches now.
- not-operator clears haveToken (token forfeited after 10 min idle) so the next command re-acquires;
  keepAlive() (control.acquire by the holder) every 60 s while Motor Test is shown and HOME/Loop/Light Scale runs.
- Motor Power sends expectRelayOn with confirmOff; no second send while one is in flight; relay-changed refusal
  is explained. (C++ must refuse when the live relay != expectRelayOn and never power ON on confirmOff:true.)
- formShow/formClose are state, not one-shot events: retried with backoff until C++ acks ok, not sent before the
  window state is known, formClose on an initial HT_WIN {open:false} (HMI reload) and on pagehide, gives up only
  when C++ does not know the action; held jogs released on close.
- MotorTest.ini: only cells loaded at FormShow are compared/written (a row shown later with '0' is never written),
  snapshot cleared when a read starts, cells zeroed on a failed read, a refused write alerts and keeps the edit
  for the next close.
- IO page: a lost socket is no longer reported as "token refused / not sent".
- cur.selectable (when C++ publishes it) decides selection, so the SIM build can select motors again.
Tests (headless Edge, scratchpad webmt): new harness4 22/0 (page), new harness5 11/0 (wire order; the same
harness on the previous commit shows control.acquire,motor.stop,motor.access and fails 7), regressions harness 40/0,
harness2 66/0, harness3 9/0; HW.teach.html loads without JS errors.

